-- הודעת תכ"ם HOD.13.4.7.1 — סכום לתשלום החזר הוצאות טלפון קווי אישי בהתאם לרמת זכאות (גרסה 1, 1.12.2008)
-- The Accountant-General's notice that prices the personal-landline
-- refund of instruction H.13.4.7: a fixed monthly sum for each entitlement
-- level, one table for a role holder who is "existing" (appointed up to
-- 30.11.2008) and one for a "new" one. The levels themselves, and who is
-- existing or new, are the instruction's (its annexes A and B), encoded in
-- its own file, which imports this one.

IMPORT prelude

-- not weighed against `the Equal Pay Law`: ‘בעל’ is ‘בעל תפקיד’, the
-- holder of a post, not a husband; the notice prices a refund of phone
-- expenses by entitlement level and makes no distinction by sex.

§ `סכום לתשלום החזר הוצאות טלפון קווי אישי בהתאם לרמת זכאות`

@desc Whether a role holder is "existing" or "new" for the personal-landline refund (annex A of instruction H.13.4.7): the notice prices the two apart.
DECLARE `landline role-holder standing` IS ONE OF
    `an existing landline role holder`
    `a new landline role holder`

@desc The entitlement level a role holder is approved at for the personal-landline refund (annex B of instruction H.13.4.7).
DECLARE `landline entitlement level` IS ONE OF
    `landline level A`
    `landline level B`
    `landline level C`
    `landline level D`

§§ `1`

-- §1 and its table: the monthly sum for an existing role holder, by the
-- level set for him under the instruction: 100.8, 139.2, 196.8 and 235.5
-- shekels for levels א to ד. (The notice cites the level as set "in
-- section 4.3.3" of instruction "13.4.0.7":
-- F-2008-12-01_takam_HOD-13-4-7-1_telefon-ramot-zakaut_v1-a.)
@ref akn:hc_1__para_1 akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_1-1 akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_1-1/t1
GIVEN l IS A `landline entitlement level`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the monthly landline sum for an existing holder under notice edition 1` l IS
    CONSIDER l
    WHEN `landline level A` THEN 100.8
    WHEN `landline level B` THEN 139.2
    WHEN `landline level C` THEN 196.8
    WHEN `landline level D` THEN 235.5

§§ `2`

-- §2 (its subsection printed "1.2") and its table: the monthly sum for a
-- new role holder, 96 shekels at level א and 144 at level ב. The table has
-- no level ג or ד, and annex B gives a new holder neither: for those the
-- notice prices nothing.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2 akn:hc_1__para_1-2 akn:hc_1__para_1-2/t1
GIVEN l IS A `landline entitlement level`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the monthly landline sum for a new holder under notice edition 1` l IS
    CONSIDER l
    WHEN `landline level A` THEN JUST 96
    WHEN `landline level B` THEN JUST 144
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- The two tables as one answer: the sum the notice sets for a holder of
-- this standing at this level, NOTHING where its tables print none.
GIVEN s IS A `landline role-holder standing`
      l IS A `landline entitlement level`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the monthly landline sum under notice edition 1` s l IS
    CONSIDER s
    WHEN `an existing landline role holder` THEN JUST (`the monthly landline sum for an existing holder under notice edition 1` l)
    WHEN `a new landline role holder` THEN `the monthly landline sum for a new holder under notice edition 1` l

-- F-2008-12-01_takam_HOD-13-4-7-1_telefon-ramot-zakaut_v1-a: the tables
-- cite the level as set "in section 4.3.3" (existing) and "in section
-- 4.4.1" (new) of takam instruction "13.4.0.7". The instruction it prices
-- is H.13.4.7 ("מס' 13.4.7", its own annex D), whose section 4 lists its
-- annexes, 4.1 to 4.5, with no clause under any of them; the levels are
-- set in its sections 2.3.3 and 2.4.1.
`the clauses section 4 of instruction 13.4.7 holds` MEANS
    LIST "4.1", "4.2", "4.3", "4.4", "4.5"
`the clauses the notice of 1.12.2008 cites` MEANS
    LIST "4.3.3", "4.4.1"
`the clauses that set the level in instruction 13.4.7` MEANS
    LIST "2.3.3", "2.4.1"
`the instruction number the notice of 1.12.2008 cites` MEANS "13.4.0.7"
`the landline instruction's number` MEANS "13.4.7"

`the notice of 1.12.2008 cites clauses instruction 13.4.7 does not hold` MEANS
        all (GIVEN c YIELD NOT elem c `the clauses section 4 of instruction 13.4.7 holds`) `the clauses the notice of 1.12.2008 cites`
    AND all (GIVEN c YIELD NOT elem c `the clauses the notice of 1.12.2008 cites`) `the clauses that set the level in instruction 13.4.7`
    AND NOT (`the instruction number the notice of 1.12.2008 cites` EQUALS `the landline instruction's number`)
#ASSERT `the notice of 1.12.2008 cites clauses instruction 13.4.7 does not hold`

§§ `Worked examples`

-- An existing holder at level ב is paid 139.2 a month and at level ד
-- 235.5; a new one at level א 96 and at level ב 144; a new holder at level
-- ג has no sum in the notice.
#ASSERT `the monthly landline sum under notice edition 1` `an existing landline role holder` `landline level B` EQUALS JUST 139.2
#ASSERT `the monthly landline sum under notice edition 1` `an existing landline role holder` `landline level D` EQUALS JUST 235.5
#ASSERT `the monthly landline sum under notice edition 1` `a new landline role holder` `landline level A` EQUALS JUST 96
#ASSERT `the monthly landline sum under notice edition 1` `a new landline role holder` `landline level B` EQUALS JUST 144
#ASSERT isNothing (`the monthly landline sum under notice edition 1` `a new landline role holder` `landline level C`)

-- The existing holders' table rises with the level, and so does the new
-- holders'.
`each landline table of 1.12.2008 rises with the level` MEANS
        `the monthly landline sum for an existing holder under notice edition 1` `landline level A`
            LESS THAN `the monthly landline sum for an existing holder under notice edition 1` `landline level B`
    AND `the monthly landline sum for an existing holder under notice edition 1` `landline level B`
            LESS THAN `the monthly landline sum for an existing holder under notice edition 1` `landline level C`
    AND `the monthly landline sum for an existing holder under notice edition 1` `landline level C`
            LESS THAN `the monthly landline sum for an existing holder under notice edition 1` `landline level D`
    AND `the monthly landline sum for a new holder under notice edition 1` `landline level A`
            LESS THAN `the monthly landline sum for a new holder under notice edition 1` `landline level B`
#ASSERT `each landline table of 1.12.2008 rises with the level`
